The thing is, most of the items in the game do
not come from random object generation.  Most
levels have only a spare handful of things on the
floor, and most of them are gold, weapons, food
gems, gold, rocks, boulders, or gold.  When you
go back to already cleared levels you don't get
more (unless you go digging, and that only nets
you more gold, gems, rocks, and gold).

Shops help a little, but large scroll shops are not
particularly common.  If you find two large scroll
shops in the same game, the RNG is leaning
more toward scroll shops than average.  Three
large scroll shops in one game would be a bit
surprising, and that would still only be about the
same number of scrolls I typically expect to
get from monsters before the castle or quest.

Thus, most of the scrolls you collect (assuming
you collect them all) are generally going to come
from monsters you or your pets have killed.  The
most common scroll type in my experience is
usually either create monster or in some games
teleportation.  Scrolls of blank paper (from paper
golems) are also consistently more common than
scrolls of light or enchant weapon.

(Tourists also seem to get an excess of scrolls
of charging, especially once they reach XL14,
but maybe that's just the RNG being mean.)

Admittedly, getting almost to the Wizard before
encountering any scrolls of enchant weapon at
all is quite a bit more spare than I have personally
experienced.  However, I've had games where I
had to go into Gehennom with a +2 or +3 main
weapon and only +0 projectiles.

I do tend to get some enchant weapon if I polypile
scrolls.  That, of course, requires a source of
polymorph, which not all games give you unless
you spend a wish on it; and also, polypiling is a
bit tedious and can cause pet maintenance issues,
especially if you're trying to keep an herbivore.


